  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected be-yad ha-mmal'akhim → by the hand of messengers: the rectum carries an article and the ASV renders messengers anarthrous with the single the before the construct, so under rule 29 that the is fronted and belongs to the article (s016), while yad takes only hand. The accepted alignment had supplied the the on the construct and left the present article unrepresented, against rule 29's direction to supply a the on a construct only where no article morpheme is present.",
